# Story: As a terminal planner, I want each container to have at most one open booking, so that two trucks are never sent for the same container. If a container already has a booking that is BOOKED, another booking for it (by anyone, for any slot) is refused with DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING. After the first booking is cancelled the container can be booked again.

@draft
Feature: Container Booking Rules

  Scenario Outline: A container can only have one open booking
    Given a gate slot tomorrow at 10:00 with room for 2 trucks
    And I book that slot for container "<container>"
    When the booking is confirmed with a reference
    Then another driver tries to book that slot for the same container
    And their booking is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"

    Examples:
      | container |
      | C1        |

  Scenario Outline: A container can be booked again after cancellation
    Given I have booked that slot for a valid container
    When another driver tries to book that slot for the same container
    And their booking is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"
    Then I cancel my booking
    And the slot has 2 places left
    And another driver books that slot for the same container
    And the booking is confirmed with a reference

    Examples:
      | container |
      | C1        |

  Scenario Outline: A container cannot be booked if it already has an active booking
    Given I book that slot for container "<container>"
    When the booking is confirmed with a reference
    Then another driver tries to book that slot for the same container
    And their booking is refused because "DUPLICATE_ACTIVE_BOOKING"

    Examples:
      | container |
